;; Command resources — CLI subcommands declared as data.
;;
;; eta-mu discovers these at startup and dispatches to their scripts, so adding
;; a subcommand needs no rebuild of the eta-mu binary.
;;
;; The boundary is data in, data out. The script receives an EDN context in
;; `ETA_MU_CONTEXT` and owns its own stdio; argv is exactly what the user typed.
;; It gets no in-process handle on eta-mu — anything it needs from eta-mu it
;; asks for by shelling back to `eta-mu ...`, which already has a published exit
;; contract. There is deliberately no injected context object to version.
;;
;; :command/runtime picks the interpreter. `bb` for repository tooling —
;; effectively instant, carries clj-yaml. `nbb` for extensions that need Node or
;; npm interop, at roughly 100ms startup.

{:namespace :eta-mu.commands

 :resources
 [{:contract/kind :command
   :contract/id "workflows"
   :command/name "workflows"
   :command/summary "Project workflow resources onto GitHub Actions and local gates"
   :command/runtime :bb
   :command/script "scripts/workflows.bb"
   :command/doc
   "Reads katamorph workflow resources from contracts/workflows/ and emits both
    .github/workflows/*.yml and the local gate plan.

    Subcommands: list, show <id>, emit [--target ...] [--dry-run], check."}]}
